# Build trees. `build-*/` covers the scratch prefixes (build-system,
# build-sdk, build-flatpak, …); build-aux/ is source and must survive it.
build/
_build/
build-*/
!build-aux/
.flatpak-builder/

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/

# Tool caches
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# Working notes, kept on disk and out of the published repository.
# CLAUDE.md is agent orientation and DECISIONS.md is the design journal:
# both are written for whoever is editing the tree, not for whoever is
# using it. CONTRIBUTING.md stays out while there are no outside
# contributors to address. docs/ is maintainer-only release procedure and
# QA status — docs/release-checklist.md in particular is a frank account of
# what has never been physically tested, and publishing it is a decision
# about the project rather than about backups.
#
# CHANGELOG.md was here too and is not any more (2026-09-02). It is not a
# working note, it is a release gate: scripts/prepare-flatpak-release.py
# checks it, that check was `if path.exists()`, and ignoring the file made
# the gate a silent no-op in every CI run while docs/publishing.md went on
# listing the changelog among the things it verifies. Tracking it and
# passing --require-changelog closes both halves.
#
# Note this leaves docs/publishing.md — the release runbook — and
# docs/release-checklist.md living on one machine with no backup. That risk
# is accepted, not solved; a private operations repository is the way to
# take it back without publishing them.
CLAUDE.md
DECISIONS.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
docs/
